{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLz3yud8w4t3k83i2HrZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] Without `go` on `PATH`, every scenario prints a TAP skip and the run exits 0.\n[x] Responses are selected by (model, turn count): reordering verifier completions in the fake does not change the result.\n[x] Injecting a one-field difference into the TS side's `meta.json` (for example a changed budget value, via a test-only fixture) makes the comparison fail and name the file and JSON path.\n[x] Injecting a different request body field on one side makes the request comparison fail and name the (model, turn count) group.\n[x] Bundle comparison reads decompressed tar entries, so two bundles with identical entries but different zstd bytes compare equal.\n[x] The CI differential job runs these scenarios on Ubuntu after `npm run build`.\n[x] Every allowlist entry used by a scenario cites the spec.md deliberate change number it relies on.\n[x] lint, typecheck, and the TS test suite pass, and the Go build and Go tests still pass.\n\nI added the six M3 review scenarios to the harness, but the first acceptance item is still open: `npm run test:diff` does not pass. All eight review cases fail on one real parity difference between the two CLIs.\n\n**The blocker:** the TS agent loop adds the `__roast_continue` nudge tool to every model request, and Go at `cd08f10` never does. Go registers the tool, but the list of tools it actually sends contains only the caller's tools. Go's own `internal/llm/provider_test.go:238` checks that a structured request carries exactly one tool. Spec 07 section 2.3 tells TS to always send the nudge, while spec 07 section 4 says the loop's behavior doesn't change from Go. It isn't one of the numbered deliberate changes, so I couldn't allowlist it. I didn't change `src/llm` either, because that's another area's specified behavior and has its own tests. I recorded it as open question 8 in `spec/07-agent-loop.md`. You need to decide one of two things:\n- **Match Go:** drop the nudge from TS requests.\n- **Keep it:** make it a numbered deliberate change, and I'd add one allowlist entry for it.\n\nEverything else already matches across all eight cases: exit codes, JSON stdout, run records, bundles, the rest of each request, and the rendered prompts.\n\n**What's in the harness now:**\n- **Scenarios** (`test/diff/scenarios/m3.ts`), all on `chat` with the finder and verifier on separate models:\n  - clean review\n  - findings confirmed by the verifier\n  - `--format json`\n  - `--staged`\n  - `--max-severity` tripping (exit 1) and not tripping\n  - HTTP 500 after retries (exit 4)\n  - HTTP 401 (exit 3)\n- **Fake server** (`test/diff/replies.ts`): each reply is chosen by model and turn count; a request with no scripted reply gets a 404 naming its key.\n- **Normalization:** these differences are expected and are now masked or skipped rather than failing:\n  - Finding IDs and aliases are random, so they're replaced.\n  - The snapshot `commit`/`ref` IDs are replaced; trees, `head` and `base` are still compared exactly.\n  - Go's SDK adds `X-Stainless-*` headers that raw fetch doesn't send, so those are ignored.\n  - gzip and zstd bytes may differ, and so do the bundle-manifest hashes of compressed files.\n  - Raw response captures are compared as parsed JSON lines, because Go escapes `<` as `\\u003c`.\n- **Self-tests** that run without Go:\n  - a review scenario compares equal against itself\n  - verifier completions arriving in opposite orders on the two sides still compare equal\n  - a changed `meta.json` budget value is reported as exactly `records/<RUN_ID>/meta.json.budgets.max_turns`\n  - an extra request-body field is reported as `requests[finder-model#3][0].body.injected`\n  - identical bundles compressed at zstd levels 1 and 19 compare equal\n\nI broke the new masking rules on purpose and the matching self-tests failed.\n\n**Checks:** `npm test` passes (7052 tests), lint and typecheck are clean, and `go build` and `go test ./...` pass. With `go` removed from `PATH`, every scenario is a TAP skip and the run exits 0.\n\n**One reading to confirm:** I left the CI job unchanged. It runs `npm run bundle`, not `npm run build`, because before M6 `npm run build` is still the Go platform build. `npm run bundle` is what produces `dist/cli.js`, and the job does run the new scenarios.\n\nThe work is in three commits. I also added harness notes to `docs/agents/typescript.md`, and the full record is in `.redeye/notes.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":151,"cache_read_input_tokens":165215,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":151},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca44731d-7017-4aec-9d20-b88aa7cfd62f","uuid":"bf2a7bba-63d1-47df-8438-8005883546ae","timestamp":"2026-11-24T02:44:03.346Z","request_id":"req_011ChLz3ykCHh5vJKqkMNw5P"}
